From e5d7f7614f9acc12058d4d1a7b0336e87fecc563 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hisi-9000c buildbot <buildbot@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:31:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: only unpin the old FB when legacy set_base pinned
 it

The legacy DCE set_base path can inherit an old framebuffer that was
not pinned by this path, for example the fbdev framebuffer at the
first modeset.  The unconditional amdgpu_bo_unpin() then hits
ttm_bo_unpin()'s WARN_ON_ONCE(!bo->pin_count) and underflows.

Drop the pin only when the old FB still has a pin.  This is the
correct boundary for the legacy path, not a global pin-lifetime fix;
the user-session startup pin-failed messages and the X11/DRI3
ttm_bo_release warning remain separate issues.

Tested on a Kirin 9000C with an Oland [1002:6611]: the session-start
ttm_bo_unpin warning is gone.  GNOME Wayland runs at 4K@30 28.8 FPS,
1080p@60 56.1 FPS, and back to 4K 29.6 FPS, with the amdgpu IRQ
counter rising across the switches and no SError/reset.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v6_0.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v6_0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v6_0.c
index 5e50cd6..4c1f802 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v6_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v6_0.c
@@ -2088,7 +2088,13 @@ static int dce_v6_0_crtc_do_set_base(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 		r = amdgpu_bo_reserve(abo, true);
 		if (unlikely(r != 0))
 			return r;
-		amdgpu_bo_unpin(abo);
+		/*
+		 * The legacy set_base path can inherit an old FB that was not
+		 * pinned here (for example the fbdev framebuffer).  Only drop
+		 * a pin this path actually holds.
+		 */
+		if (abo->tbo.pin_count)
+			amdgpu_bo_unpin(abo);
 		amdgpu_bo_unreserve(abo);
 	}
 
